        { "id": "heatmap-chart-diverging", "title": "Diverging colors", "lead": "For values on either side of a meaningful middle, such as each month's temperature against the normal, set `Palette` to `ChartPalette.Diverging` with a color for each side. The scale turns gray at `Midpoint` (0 by default).", "after": ["The scale reaches as far on both sides, so colors of the same strength mean the same distance from the middle. `Steps` sets about how many classes there are (5 by default); here the bounds round to four classes of 2°C, two on each side.", "`Legend=\"ChartLegend.End\"` stands the scale upright beside the grid, with the high end at the top."] },
