      "examples": [
        { "id": "drop-zone-group-board", "title": "A board", "lead": "To move items between lists, put a `ListView` with a `Zone` in the group for each column, anywhere in its layout. The group owns the items, and `ZoneOf` returns the zone each one is in.", "after": ["To show a list's items as cards, set `Cards` on its `ListView`.", "On interactive pages, `@bind-Items` keeps the order, and `OnMove` (with `FromZone` and `ToZone`) is where you save a move.", "On static pages, give the group a `Name` and pass the posted `ListOrder` back as `Order`. `SubmitOnMove` posts each move, and `Order.Arrange` gives each item's zone and place to save.", "To limit what a zone accepts, set `Accepts` and `MaxItems`. The Kanban board demo shows them, with cards that drag from anywhere."],
          "notes": {
